        <dcterms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Winstonpartwhole Pattern</dcterms:title>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x10; term declared x2;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Winstonpartwhole Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-component&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-component o po-component) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-feature&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-feature o po-feature) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-member&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-member o po-member) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-place&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-place o po-place) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-portion&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-portion o po-portion) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- axiom removed: AsymmetricObjectProperty(&lt;http://daselab.org/WinstonPartWhole#po-stuff&gt;) - asymmetry on a property that is transitive (its chain po-stuff o po-stuff) is outside OWL 2 DL, so no reasoner could answer; the chains carry the pattern&apos;s inferences and stay
- file: pattern.owl written as RDF/XML - it held Turtle
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


